  "summary": "A San Diego City Council committee will consider a resolution by councilmember Henry Foster III to terminate the city's contract with Flock Safety, delete stored ALPR data, and rescind SDPD's ALPR policy. A new council majority appears to support cancellation, though Mayor Todd Gloria, a Flock supporter, could veto. The resolution cites a wrongful arrest, a data-sharing breach, and a pending ACLU lawsuit.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "If passed, Foster's proposal calls for the termination of the city's contract with Flock Safety, and for the city to delete all stored data along with it.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "On Sept. 30, the ACLU Foundation of San Diego & Imperial Counties filed a lawsuit against the city of San Diego, claiming the technology violates the California Constitution's stated right to privacy",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    },
    {
      "quote": "If Flock cameras are causing many San Diegans to feel unsafe, then they have lost effectiveness as a public safety tool.",
      "paragraph_idx": 12
    }
  ],
